From ed8341821a1e7c1a1db168faf8ba256ed6784e67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sagar Cheluvegowda <quic_scheluve@quicinc.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Oct 2025 18:09:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/28] PENDING: net: stmmac: Add NULL check for match data

The qcom_ethqos_probe() function retrieves platform-specific data
using of_device_get_match_data(). The returned pointer is then
dereferenced without a preceding NULL check.

If a new device is added to the of_device_id table without a
corresponding .data field, of_device_get_match_data() will return
NULL. This leads to a kernel panic from a NULL pointer dereference
on the subsequent line.

This commit adds a check to validate the data pointer immediately
after the call. If the pointer is NULL, an error is logged and the
probe function returns -ENODEV, preventing the crash and providing
clear feedback for debugging.

This ensures the driver probes safely and handles missing platform
data gracefully.

Change-Id: Id997429aa24032565b7e0c13a82daa901bca0a89
Signed-off-by: Sagar Cheluvegowda <quic_scheluve@quicinc.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c
index 458dde1d0e2a7..bef2e58ec5149 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c
@@ -932,6 +932,11 @@ static int qcom_ethqos_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	data = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
 	ethqos->rgmii_por = data->rgmii_por;
 	ethqos->num_rgmii_por = data->num_rgmii_por;
+	if (!data) {
+		dev_err(dev, "No match data found\n");
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	ethqos->has_io_macro_ge_4 = data->has_io_macro_ge_4;
 	ethqos->rgmii_config_loopback_en = data->rgmii_config_loopback_en;
 	ethqos->has_emac_ge_3 = data->has_emac_ge_3;
